Sampling profiler: PS2X_PROFILE=2 says who called the system code a sample lands in, and PS2X_PROFILE=3 which source lines are hot. For a sample outside the executable (the heap, memcpy, locks, waits) mode 2 unwinds the stack with the x64 unwind data while the thread is still suspended, up to the first four return addresses inside the executable, and every 15 seconds prints the hottest call chains per thread after the usual report ([profile:callers], "leaf <- caller <- its caller ..."). Mode 3 prints the hottest file:line per thread from the PDB's line table ([profile:lines]; MSVC counts code it inlined at the line of the call). PS2X_PROFILE=1 is unchanged. In Metropolismania's city mode 2 showed the game thread's heap time as operator new in the GS command queue's push, its memmove as DMA chain buffers growing, and its waits as the GS queue drain before a frame buffer clear; mode 3 showed texture sampling and pixel writes as the band threads' hottest lines. Runs are as fast as with PS2X_PROFILE=1.

